Z||000006||Black88GT||09-10-2001||12:35 AM||||Baseball umps do about 160 games a year.  NFL only does 18 at the most.  <P><BR>I don't disagree that they deserve a raise.  I don't think anyone will debate that.  However, 400% is ridiculous, and they should have taken the NFL's last offer which I just found out is 60% this year, and doubled in 3 years (I was wrong in my first post).||||reg||1
Z||000007||firstfiero||09-10-2001||06:56 AM||||      No way they deserve the same pay as refs from other weeks. I don't care how long they study films! They only officiate 17 games. A couple more if their a good group and they get picked for the playoffs. One of those guys actually had the nerve to say when asked "What makes you believe you deserve to get paid as much as an assistant coach"....."Well we work almost 30 hrs a week" The coach just laughed at him and walk away. Your average assistant coach doesn't make 200 grand a year and puts in 16 hr work days on average. These officials want 211 grand a year! Nuts!<BR>   Anyway...they did a good job in the cowboys game. Missed one or two calls in both directions. <BR>    All I got to say is the better look at the major league umps and see the leson they learned. The game is about the players and the fans not about zebra's.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
